  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) have taken disciplinary action against two high-ranking officials found guilty of participating in a conspiracy to wiretap President Prabowo Subianto. According to official reports, the accused utilized police equipment to conduct the surveillance activities. Inspector General Eko Hadi Santoso was among those issued a dishonorable discharge. During the ethics proceeding, the official presented mitigating witnesses but ultimately expressed regret and issued an apology for his conduct. Despite the dismissal decision, Eko Hadi has initiated an appeal process. Meanwhile, the scope of the investigation continues to expand, with authorities confirming that a former National Police Chief will undergo an ethics hearing next week as part of the broader inquiry into the breach. Polri leadership has emphasized that no personnel, regardless of rank, will be exempt from accountability in this case.",
